{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat -n '/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790808000000-orchestrator-linker-over-dht-owner-decisions.md'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Linker over dao.jing.dht — OWNER DECISIONS (2026-10-01)\n     2\t\n     3\tInputs:\n     4\t- Lead design (fable): collab/1790806000000-architect-linker-over-dht.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md\n     5\t- Second opinion (gpt-6-sol, AGREE-WITH-CHANGES): collab/1790806000000-architect-linker-over-dht-second-opinion.gpt-6-sol.findings.md\n     6\t\n     7\tOwner answers (verbatim selections):\n     8\t1. Rows: \"Every round\". Materialize every evaluated program's rows into the index store each round (fable's recommendation; gpt-6-sol disagreed). This also settles the :yin/address contract: an index address fact names retrievable content.\n     9\t2. Keys: \"Loaded from a file (stable)\". A durable publisher identity, with key loss and replacement behaviour to be defined. Tests may use ephemeral keys.\n    10\t3. Dart: \"Add Ed25519 for Dart now\". Signed name resolution on JVM, Node and Dart, with cross-host signature vectors.\n    11\t4. Same name, same address from two declared principals: \"Consensus: resolve\" (the current fold behaviour). Different addresses still refuse as ambiguous.\n    12\t\n    13\tAdopted as the Architects' shared recommendation (the orchestrator stated these; the owner did not object):\n    14\t- Explicit named-export publication, derived from indexed code.\n    15\t- A configured DHT link source may start a bounded load on require; the banner and help say so; pending and failure are data.\n    16\t- Names come from explicitly loaded snapshots only.\n    17\t- Deferred: the persistent stepped ring linker, latest-root discovery, and the lease link policy.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
