{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat -n '/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790806000000-architect-linker-over-dht.prompt.md'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Architect design pass: load and evaluate code from dao.jing.dht via the linker\n     2\t\n     3\tRole: Lead System Architect (docs/agents/roles/architect.md). This is a read-only DESIGN pass on master (c66809fa). Do not edit code.\n     4\tLead: claude-fable-5-1. A second opinion from gpt-6-sol or gemini follows.\n     5\t\n     6\t## Owner request\n     7\tQueued by the owner on 2026-10-01, after this exchange. The owner asked whether another yin.repl attached to the same dao.jing.dht can use dao.space.query to query stored code AND load that code for evaluation. The answer was: querying yes (S5); loading for evaluation no. Those are separate paths:\n     8\t- The code index is datoms plus a manifest, in the `--index-store`.\n     9\t- The linker (yin.repl.link, yin.vm.linker.md) resolves name → manifest address through a name environment, and links module images over a dao.jing content pair (`:content-store` / `:content-client`).\n    10\tOwner, verbatim: \"queue the linker design pass after S5\".\n    11\t\n    12\t## Binding owner invariants\n    13\t- \"plain clojure code should be able to query for code in the dht. the yin.repl should use the same path as the clojure repl via host-functions\" (2026-10-01). Any load path must be a plain-Clojure API that yin.repl reuses through host functions.\n    14\t- Share code over the stream linker: the linker boundary is dao.stream, and local vs remote linking is just a stream. See memory notes project_invariant_share_code_over_stream_linker and project_linker_is_stream_boundary, summarized in docs.\n    15\t- dao.stream is P2P: no server/client, no privileged node, NAT-traversing in principle.\n    16\t- Derive, don't persist: do not add structure a Datalog query over existing rows can derive.\n    17\t- dao.jing is syntax and agents are semantics: the store stays passive and payload-agnostic.\n    18\t- Code and continuations are datoms.\n    19\t\n    20\t## Questions to answer\n    21\t1. **Content source.** How the DHT becomes the linker's content source. Is it a DHT-backed `:content-client` over the `:jing/*` convention? How does it relate to `dao.space.dht/join`?\n    22\t2. **What gets published.** Linkable module images, the code index, or both? Can the linker's image be DERIVED from the code index (datoms), or is it a separate artifact? Judge this against derive-don't-persist.\n    23\t3. **Naming and discovery.** How does a second process learn name → manifest address? Weigh:\n    24\t   - an index-derived name environment (a query over `:yin/name` datoms in a loaded index);\n    25\t   - a published name-environment root;\n    26\t   - handing addresses over some other way.\n    27\t   Root or latest-root discovery was out of the DHT epic's scope; say what the minimal honest step is and what stays deferred.\n    28\t4. **Authority and trust.** yin.vm.linker.authority exists. Who may bind a name? What stops a peer from shadowing a name? How does the ShiBi capability direction (memory: ShiBi is a tuple space) bear on it?\n    29\t5. **Evaluation semantics.**\n    30\t   - How loaded code enters a receiving session's VM: link-policy, pending links, lease.\n    31\t   - Across all four VMs.\n    32\t   - Failure outcomes as data.\n    33\t6. **Slices.** A slice plan with acceptance criteria and the files each slice touches. Include a REPL end-to-end:\n    34\t   - process A defines functions and publishes;\n    35\t   - process B joins, loads by name, and evaluates;\n    36\t   - plain Clojure does the same through the same API.\n    37\t7. **OWNER decisions.** Anything that needs the owner's call.\n    38\t\n    39\t## Read first\n    40\t- docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md\n    41\t- docs/design/yin.repl.link-policy.md\n    42\t- docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.linker.md\n    43\t- docs/design/dao.jing.dht.md\n    44\t- docs/design/yin.repl.dao.space-index.md\n    45\t- src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc\n    46\t- src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc\n    47\t- src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc\n    48\t- src/cljc/yin/vm/linker*.cljc\n    49\t- collab/1790795000000-repl-engineer-dht-s5-repl-integration.claude-opus-5-5.report*.md\n    50\t\n    51\tOutput: a findings document with the sections above, ending in a slice plan and a list of OWNER decisions.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
